-- title:
--   Normalized upper bound: $f(x_N) - f(0) \le \tau_N \|r\|^2$
-- statement:
--   Let $f : E \to \mathbb{R}$ be a normalized admissible function — convex, differentiable, with globally $1$-Lipschitz gradient, and with $f(0) = 0$, $\nabla f(0) = 0$ and $0$ a global minimizer, i.e. the normalizations $x^\star = 0$, $f^\star = 0$, $L = 1$ of §1 — let $r$ be the initial point and let $N \ge 1$. Then the output of the rational-momentum Nesterov method satisfies
--   $$ f(x_N) - f(0) \;\le\; \tau_N\,\|r\|^{2}, \qquad \tau_N = \frac{2}{N^2+7N+4}, $$
--   where $x_N$ is the final extrapolated iterate (3.2) obtained by running the method with step $1$ from $x_0 = r$, and $\|r\|$ is the distance from the initial point to the optimizer.
--
--   This is the all-$N$ bound (1.1)/(17.1) of Theorem A in normalized coordinates. Its content is a positivity statement about the certificate rather than a direct analytic estimate: the master identity (7.1) writes $\tau_N\|r\|^2 - f(x_N)$ as a sum of interpolation residuals and squares, so the inequality follows without discarding anything but signs.
--
--   The boundary case $N = 1$ is the separate exact identity (18.1) of §18, whose right-hand constant is precisely $\tau_1 = 1/6$, so the two regimes join with no gap; §19 then restores the general $L, R$ statement, which is what makes this lemma the upper half of Theorem B.
-- source:
--   《有理动量 Nesterov 紧界与半径归一化五算法共同最坏情形 — 可审计完整证明稿》 (manuscript, 2026-10-08), §1, eq. (1.1) and §17, eq. (17.1) (boundary case §18, eq. (18.1); master certificate §7, eq. (7.1)); Lean: FullFormalization.TheoremA lines 68-242

